##  TypeScript End-User API for 3D Camera Animation (Prioritizing Helpfulness & Verbosity)

This API aims to be intuitive, flexible, and robust for controlling 3D camera animations in TypeScript, balancing ease of use with powerful customization options.

**Core Concepts & Structure:**

1. **`CameraController` Class:** The central hub managing camera behavior. Instances represent individual cameras within your scene.

   ```typescript
   class CameraController {
       constructor(target: THREE.Object3D, initialPosition: Vector3, initialRotation: Vector3) {
           this.target = target; // Object the camera orbits/tracks
           this.position = initialPosition;
           this.rotation = initialRotation;
           this.animationQueue = []; // Stores queued animations
       }

       // Animation Methods (detailed below)
       animateTo(targetPos: Vector3, duration: number, easing?: EasingFunction): this;
       smoothTrack(targetObj: THREE.Object3D, duration: number, orbitRadius: number, easing?: EasingFunction): this;
       createDollyZoom(initialDistance: number, finalDistance: number, duration: number, easing?: EasingFunction): this;
       // ... more advanced techniques (pan, swing, spring, etc.)

       start(): void; // Initiates queued animations sequentially
       stop(): void;    // Clears and halts active animations
       pauseResume(): void; // Pauses/Resumes ongoing animations
       getAnimationProgress(): number; // Returns progress (0-1) of current animation
   }
   ```

2. **Animation Types & Fluent API:**

   * **`animateTo(targetPos, duration, easing)`:**  Directly moves the camera to a specified position over a given duration, using optional easing functions for smooth transitions (linear, easeInOut, etc.).

   * **`smoothTrack(targetObj, duration, orbitRadius, easing)`:**  Makes the camera smoothly orbit/follow a moving object while maintaining a consistent radius. Ideal for character or object tracking.

   * **`createDollyZoom(initialDistance, finalDistance, duration, easing)`:**  Simulates a cinematic dolly zoom effect, changing both camera distance and field of view concurrently.

   * **Extensibility:**  Allow adding custom animation blueprints (functions)  for unique effects, enabling users to define their own behaviors and composition.

